& [ProviderNeutralContract] is shared rather than duplicated
  + SharedAttentionToolRequest closes all eleven validation transition settlement and imagination operations
  + SharedAttentionToolResult retains exact operation-specific machine forms without adding a new wire wrapper
  + SharedAttentionToolResponse retains the original JSON shell profile field shape exit meanings fault structure and three nonclaims
  + one execute_shared_attention_tool_request function delegates only to the already verified pure runtime

& [SchemaSolution] is derived from executable types
  + every reachable shared-attention form has optional JsonSchema capability beside its existing strict serde form
  + FacultyKind SemanticId and ContentDigest participate in the same reachable schema graph
  + the MCP input schema is the closed CoordinateAttentionArguments wrapper and output schema is the complete shared response
  + operation inventory and deterministic metadata are tested from live generated definitions

& [CliSolution] is a thin compatibility transport
  + cantor-shared-attention now owns only argument parsing bounded process input response writing diagnostics and exit projection
  + the CLI no longer maintains its own operation enum dispatch response status or semantic serialization path
  + validate applied buffered and stale-refusal calls compare exactly with direct dispatch JSON

& [McpSolution] is one stateless standard tool
  + cantor-shared-attention-mcp exposes coordinate_attention over STDIO with no startup state or configuration file
  + one complete request is required under request and encoded arguments are bounded to 32 MiB
  + structuredContent carries the complete response while text is a short non-authoritative summary
  + succeeded and buffered are MCP success while refused invalid_request and internal_fault retain structured content with the MCP error flag
  + annotations declare read-only non-destructive idempotent and closed-world behavior

& [InferenceUse] is an ordinary later-pass tool loop
  + a host presents exact state receives one exact successor backpressure or refusal and may show that response to a later model pass
  + state is never inserted into a token generation already in progress
  + server instructions require exact digests epistemic labels faults backpressure and nonclaims to survive reentry

& [Noninterference] is explicit
  + query_sop and route_attention remain distinct unchanged tools
  + no host registration model invocation network listener frame store session authority signing key external effect or llama.cpp change occurs

& [Disposition] is implemented_verified_stateless_adapter_P0
